\page configuration Configuration

Nocterm allocates most of its internal buffers statically (e.g. I/O buffers, key event buffers, widget text buffers). Each of these buffers has a sane default size, defined as a `NOCTERM_*` macro inside the relevant header file.

If the default sizes do not fit the needs of your application (e.g. you need longer button labels, or a deeper widget tree), these limits can be overridden at build time via the project's `Kconfig`-based configuration system, without editing any header file.

---

# Using menuconfig

The configuration menu is opened with:

```shell
make menuconfig
```

> This requires a Kconfig frontend to be installed, such as `kconfiglib` (`pip install kconfiglib`), which provides the `kconfig-mconf` and `kconfig-conf` tools used by the makefile.

Inside the menu, options are grouped under **Core** and **Widgets** categories. Each group of related limits is hidden behind a `menuconfig` toggle named `Override ... limits`. Enabling such a toggle reveals the individual numeric options belonging to that group.

`Example`

To change the maximum text size of the button widget:

1. Run `make menuconfig`.
2. Enter the **Widgets** menu.
3. Enable `Override button limits`.
4. Set `Maximum button text size (characters)` to the desired value.
5. Save and exit.

Once saved, an internal configuration header is (re)generated and automatically included for every subsequent `make` invocation. Any limit whose group toggle is left disabled keeps using its built-in default value.

---

# How It Works

Every overridable limit is defined in its header using the following pattern:

```c
#ifndef CONFIG_NOCTERM_EXAMPLE_LIMIT
    #define NOCTERM_EXAMPLE_LIMIT 128
#else
    #define NOCTERM_EXAMPLE_LIMIT CONFIG_NOCTERM_EXAMPLE_LIMIT
#endif
```

If `make menuconfig` was never run, or the corresponding `Override ... limits` toggle is disabled, `CONFIG_NOCTERM_EXAMPLE_LIMIT` is never defined and the hardcoded default is used. Otherwise, the value chosen in `menuconfig` takes precedence.

> If you are not building from source with the project's `configure`/`make` workflow (Refer to \ref installation), none of the `CONFIG_NOCTERM_*` macros will be defined, and Nocterm always falls back to its built-in defaults.


---

# Available Options

## Core

| Configuration                            | Description                                            | Default | Group Toggle                  |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------ |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_WIDGET_MAX_DEPTH`          | Maximum widget tree depth                               | 128     | `NOCTERM_WIDGET_LIMITS`         |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_IO_BUFFER_SIZE`            | I/O buffer size (bytes)                                 | 8192    | `NOCTERM_IO_LIMITS`             |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_KEY_BUFFER_SIZE`           | Key event buffer size (bytes)                           | 256     | `NOCTERM_KEY_LIMITS`            |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_KEY_ESCSEQ_INTERVAL`       | Escape sequence next-character wait interval (ms)       | 50      | `NOCTERM_KEY_LIMITS`            |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER_SIZE`     | Attribute escape sequence buffer size (bytes)           | 512     | `NOCTERM_ATTRIBUTE_LIMITS`      |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_TIMER_CALLBACK_MOMENTARY_MAX` | Maximum momentary timer callbacks                    | 64      | `NOCTERM_TIMER_LIMITS`          |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_OVERLAY_WIDGET_MAX_SIZE`   | Maximum widgets per overlay                             | 16      | `NOCTERM_OVERLAY_LIMITS`        |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_PAGE_TITLE_MAX_SIZE`       | Maximum page title size (characters)                    | 256     | `NOCTERM_PAGE_LIMITS`           |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_PAGE_STACK_MAX_SIZE`       | Maximum page stack size                                 | 128     | `NOCTERM_PAGE_LIMITS`           |

## Widgets

| Configuration                                  | Description                                       | Default | Group Toggle                |
| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------- |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_BUTTON_TEXT_MAX_SIZE`             | Maximum button text size (characters)                | 256     | `NOCTERM_BUTTON_LIMITS`        |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_DECORBOX_LABEL_MAX_SIZE`          | Maximum decorbox label size (characters)             | 64      | `NOCTERM_DECORBOX_LIMITS`      |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_ENTRY_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE`            | Maximum entry buffer size (characters)               | 4096    | `NOCTERM_ENTRY_LIMITS`         |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_TEXTBOX_BUFFER_MAX_SIZE`          | Maximum textbox buffer size (characters)             | 8192    | `NOCTERM_TEXTBOX_LIMITS`       |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_TEXTVIEW_BUFFER_SIZE`             | Maximum textview buffer size (characters)            | 8096    | `NOCTERM_TEXTVIEW_LIMITS`      |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_LISTVIEW_ITEM_CONTENT_MAX_SIZE`   | Maximum listview item content size (characters)      | 1024    | `NOCTERM_LISTVIEW_LIMITS`      |
| `CONFIG_NOCTERM_MENU_ITEM_CONTENT_MAX_SIZE`       | Maximum menu item content size (characters)          | 128     | `NOCTERM_MENU_LIMITS`          |
